Do you not understand that it would be so phenomenally unlikely that
one could exhaust _all_ of the finite resources in NetHack (by
extincting every monster and fully exploring every level) and still
have no means of uncursing? One would have to find no usable altars
(and have minetown bones with the altar destroyed), never found a
remove curse scroll or holy water (or a polymorph method) and fully
exhaust every fountain in the dungeon. And that's just for starters.

Frankly I'm not even sure that anyone has found bones without a
minetown altar. Let alone that they didn't find seven candles or some
other wish source. Let alone that in that game the castle wand was
generated cursed (1/34 chance). Let alone that they never found a
scroll of remove curse in all the deathdrops from the finite but huge
amount of monsters in the game. Let alone that they used up every
fountain trying to uncurse the wand. Let alone that cursed wands are
usable the vast majority of the time anyway.

Yes, it is _concievable_ that one could be left with a truly
unwinnable game due to lack of candles if pudding farming and infintie
quest monsters were removed. However this is so _astronomically
unlikely_ that that possibility is really no price at all to pay for
fixing those things, if one believes they need fixing.



